  "raw": {
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Goucher-College-Campus/Grant-Program-Assistant_R-0000000854": {
      "title": "Grant Program Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: The Grant Program Assistant supports the implementation and daily operations of the Next Generation Scholars program and College Preparation Intervention Program (CPIP) – comprehensive college preparation initiatives serving Baltimore City Schools and Baltimore County Public Schools. This role coordinates student services, manages program logistics, and provides direct support to participants and families while working collaboratively with campus partners, high school partners, and community-based organizations. Essential Job Functions: 20  %          A.  Student Services Coordination – Manage participant recruitment, application review, and ongoing student support services, including tutoring coordination and academic progress monitoring. 20  %          B.   Program Operations – Coordinate transportation logistics, campus visits, family engagement events, and Summer Academy residential programming for 100 students across four or five Baltimore City and Baltimore County high schools. 20  %          C.  Event Planning – Organize and execute monthly campus programming, family workshops, college visits, and special events while ensuring compliance with safety and institutional policies. 20  %          D. Partnership Liaison – Serve as the primary contact with Goucher campus partners, Baltimore City Schools, and Baltimore County Public Schools personnel, community partners, and family members, providing bilingual communication support as needed.  20 %           E.   Data Management – Maintain comprehensive student tracking systems, prepare progress reports, and support program evaluation efforts using Slate and other database systems. Education: Required:  Bachelor’s degree in education, social work, or related field Preferred: Master’s degree Professional Experience: Required: One year of administrative or program/event management experience in college access programming, student services, or K-12 education, or related field Experience working with first-generation college students and the underrepresented population Preferred: Experience with Baltimore City Schools or urban education environments Knowledge of the college admission and financial aid process Event planning and logistics coordination experience Experience working with diverse, multilingual families Bilingual Reading, Writing, and Speaking Skills (Spanish / English) Proficiency in database management systems and/or CRM (Slate) . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $17.00-$20.00 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Goucher-College-Campus/Capital-Project-Manager_R-0000000850": {
      "title": "Capital Project Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Capital Projects Manager reports directly to the Senior Vice President (SVP) for Finance and Operations and has primary responsibility for ensuring the timely and cost-effective development and completion of all campus capital projects. Essential Job Functions: 45% A. Manage Capital Project Portfolio and Delivery: Provide regular progress reports for all capital projects. Regularly identify and manage project dependencies and critical path activities.  Routinely validate project schedules, monitor project cost controls, resolve coordination issues across the College’s portfolio of projects. Manage the process for reviewing and monitoring project submittals, Requests For Information (RFIs) logs, Architectural / Engineering Clarifications (AECs), and preliminary and final As-Built Drawings for compliance with project requirements. Establish and ensure adherence to policies and procedures for new project management standards. Promote sustainable practices across all project delivery methods. Monitor project deliverables for compliance with project requirements. Review construction drawings and specifications; attend pre-bid and bid opening meetings to discuss principal construction features and requirements relating to means and methods; and inform contractors of requirements concerning easements, rights-of-way, and utility services. Attend and proactively participate in project meetings with contractors, design & engineering professionals, and constituent groups. Guide meeting outcomes and decisions towards alignment with the College’s Campus Master Plan and any fiscal constraints posed by its capital improvement plan. Inform contractors of requirements for construction scheduling, progress reporting, safety measures, wage and hour law observances, labor relations, and payroll records. Assist the SVP in understanding current industry trends or future College space needs, generating recommendations for consideration by senior leadership. Lead management of technical aspects for assigned projects, including major repair and maintenance efforts performed by the College’s Facilities Management Services (FMS) team.   25% B. Lead the development of project scopes, budgets, and schedules.  Manage the design phase for all capital projects, including organizing and supervising competitive selection of architects and other consultants as required. Coordinate consultant and stakeholder meetings and activities to ensure institutional goals and regulatory requirements are met. Manage value engineering and/or scope reduction activities as needed to ensure budget compliance. 15% C. Supervise inspection of construction operations for compliance with design intent and specifications. Interpret plans and specifications and confer with contractor representatives to resolve differences of opinions with the design team. Prepare cost estimates and schedules for all capital projects, including new construction, rehabilitation, infrastructure, energy performance, remodeling, mechanical / electrical / plumbing, fire protection, or general repair projects. Coordinate construction operations with any Baltimore County and/or State of Maryland agencies involved in the renovation and construction of college buildings. 10% D. Oversee and manage design professionals in establishing design guidelines, building programs capable of ensuring academic space requirements are met, and identifying the scope and budget parameters of future capital projects. The selected candidate will also be responsible for providing information needed to support fundraising activities. Education: Required: Bachelor's degree or appropriate certification in Engineering, Construction Management, , Project Management certification, or other relevant field of study. Professional Experience: Required: Ten (10) years of related experience in project management, construction management, and/or program management in the construction or building industry. Experience should include contract negotiations and supervision/oversight of construction activities. Strong knowledge of design, construction, and state and local building codes. Candidate must have a proven ability to work independently and be comfortable as both a team leader and team member. Preferred: Prior Supervisory and leadership experience. Experience working within a campus or academic environment. Experience with contract negotiation. 5% Provide policy and technical recommendations to the SVP as well as supporting departments, contractors, and vendors concerning the construction, renovation, and refurbishment of campus structures. . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $125,000.00-$148,000.00 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Goucher-College-Campus/PT-Campus-Safety_R-0000000845": {
      "title": "PT Campus Safety",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: The Campus Safety Officer serves as the first point of contact for community members and visitors accessing Goucher’s campus. The Campus Safety Officer is responsible for maintaining safety and security on Goucher’s campus, primarily through access control. Employees will be assigned to evening, night, or rotating shifts, including holidays and weekends. They may also be called in for overtime as needed. Officers must be prepared to work outdoors in all weather conditions and be available for duty at all hours to ensure the continuous operation of the agency. Additional responsibilities include managing security at high-profile and campus-wide events, ensuring attendee safety, coordinating with event staff, and monitoring activities. Officers may also be tasked with building watch, overseeing access control, crowd management, and addressing security concerns during events. Essential Job Functions: 30  % A.  Greet and assist guests and visitors entering the campus, providing friendly and informative assistance. Monitor and enforce access control procedures to ensure only authorized personnel and visitors enter the premises. At specified times, log all visitors entering and leaving the campus, accurately recording necessary details. 30  % B.   Maintain a vigilant presence, continuously observing surroundings and promptly addressing any security concerns or breaches. Monitor CCTV systems to oversee campus activities, traffic and identify any suspicious behavior or incidents. 15  % C.   Communicate effectively via radio with security team members and relevant personnel to coordinate responses and share information. Communicate and maintain good relationships with faculty, staff, students, other law enforcement agencies and public officials.  10 % D. Check emails and other communication channels regularly to stay updated on campus events, security alerts, and operational changes. 5 % E.  Prepare and submit detailed reports on incidents, property damage and any security-related matters as required. 5% F. Support student worker program by training and working alongside individuals for events and activities. Education: Required:   High School diploma Preferred: Associates Degree Professional Experience: Required: 1 years Customer Service Experience Preferred:   2 years of Security, Greeter, Front Desk Experience In accordance with Maryland Senate Bill 760 (2023), any individual employed as a security guard or loss prevention personnel must be licensed as a security guard. Employment in this role is contingent upon obtaining and maintaining a valid Maryland Security Guard Certification. A valid driver's license is required. This position will work Sunday and Monday from 3:00 p.m. to 11:00 p.m. every other weekend. . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $18.00-$21.00 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
    },
    "https://goucher.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Facilities/Temporary-Environmental-Technician_R-0000000844": {
      "title": "Temporary Environmental Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: A highly customer service-oriented position that is supervised by the Associate Director and Supervisors of Environmental Services. The position is responsible for performing the cleaning tasks required for the upkeep and cleanliness of college buildings and will assist the supervisor in the assignment and direction of work as required.       10% A.   Vacuum, spot clean upholstered furniture using vacuum cleaner and/or brush. Clean baseboards. 10 %   B.    Sweep and mop stairs, landings by hand or machine. 10 %   C.     Clean offices, classrooms, public areas and restrooms. 10 %    D.    Clean and dust furniture, bulletin cases, pictures, fixtures, door frames, and related furnishings. 10 %   E.    Clean, sanitize and disinfect restrooms. Replenish paper and soap supplies. 10 % F.    Collect and carry out trash and recyclable material. 10 %   G.   Perform snow removal as assigned. 10 %   H.   Communicate to the supervisor about any maintenance problems in the assigned areas. 10 %    I.   Assist the supervisor with the inspection of work in the assigned buildings to ensure standards are being met. 10 % J. Perform other duties as assigned. Education: Required: Combination of training, experience and education directly related to custodial cleaning. Preferred: High school diploma or equivalency. Professional Experience: Required: One year of custodial experience. The starting salary for this position is $15.89. . Job Category: Staff Pay Range: $15.58-$16.58 . Goucher Benefits Information . Application Instructions: Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   Please submit the following application materials:   Cover Letter    Resume   3 references   Goucher College is an Equal Opportunity Employer   Candidates must be able to provide proof of eligibility to work in the USA. No Visa sponsorship is offered for this position.   Goucher College is committed to increasing the equity of our community and seeks applicants dedicated to applying principles of equity and inclusion in all areas of the campus community."
